Topic 11 – Classes and Objects
Objective: Object creation, reference variables, instance members, state and behaviour, object interaction.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	Employee Object	Create an Employee class with ID, name and salary. Create an object and display its details.
02	Student Object	Create a Student class with name, roll number and marks. Create an object and display the data.
03	Bank Account	Create a BankAccount class with balance and methods to deposit and display balance.
04	Calculator Object	Create a Calculator class with instance methods for arithmetic operations.
05	Multiple Objects	Create three Employee objects with different data and display their details.
06	Car Object	Create a Car class with brand, model and speed. Create methods to accelerate and display speed.
07	Object Interaction	Create a Login class and a Dashboard class. Invoke a Dashboard method after calling the Login method from a separate runner class.
08	Book Objects	Create a Book class and create multiple book objects with different details.
09	Object as Parameter	Create a method that accepts an Employee object as a parameter and prints its details.
10	Object Return	Create a method that creates and returns a Student object. Invoke the method and display the returned object's details.